{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332796-magic-crafting-speciality","id":1332796,"title":"Magic crafting speciality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-27T03:16:28-07:00","id":1332796,"title":"Magic crafting speciality","content":"Hello mages!<br /> <br /> In my current (and first) campaign of MtA (second edition), one of my player want to focus the capabilities of his character on the magical crafting.<br /> So, he take the Obrimos Path ( because i told him that Prime would be a must-have for creating Imbue Items later) and max out the Prime Arcana (for a Gnose 1 character).<br /> <br /> But, he fells very frustated during the first play ( where i introduced the rules of magic) when i told him all mages can enhance or add magical property to items with all the Arcana. I think he thought it was a rare pratice, and because he is only Gnose 1, he hadn't the &quot;Imbue Item&quot; Attainement, and cannot create something &quot;unique&quot; for the moment.<br /> <br /> The SoS supplement adds some pretty cool rules with the &quot;Stored Spell&quot; spell and the alternatives, so it saves the day a little. But because of this situation, i was thinking about a way to add a sort of specialty on magical crafting to a character. Like a merit perhaps, because a Gnose 1 character hadn't much options like join a legacy.<br /> <br /> Did you have any ideas about creating a mean to do that ( I'm particulary interested about how to balance this) ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25586-erebe","name":"Erebe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25586_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T05:30:07-07:00","id":1332805,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Imbue Item&quot; attainment is gained when a character reaches Prime 4. Then the mage can use it to store a spell of any Arcanum into an item, but Prime 4 is a prequisite. Your player needs to reach Gnosis 3 to be able to get to Prime 4.<br /> <br /> At character creation he can start with a Gnosis of up to 3, if he spends all 10 of his merit points to do so. Also, he can begin the game with 3 dots in Prime. So, a starting character easily get to Prime 4 with his first 4 experiences. If you feel that having a starting character with Gnosis 3 is too much, then yeah he will need to wait a bit. If you don't though, you can let him start with Gnosis 3 and Prime 3 and have him role-play a few scenes where he is trying to learn how to Imbue Items. Maybe the procedure goes wrong, maybe it fails, maybe he causes paradox as he's trying to reach a level of power beyond his limits. Then, a few sessions in, he can increase his Prime and finally manage to do it.<br /> <br /> Concerning whether it's a rare practice or not: In the books it's not described as such. It is available to every mage with Prime 4. However , how many mages actually manage to reach Prime 4 is entirely up to you. Maybe in your game, getting to a 4th dot in an Arcanum is extremely difficult and only the most talented mages can do it. Then, if your player does so, he will be one of the few that have pulled this off.<br /> <br /> What you can do to make your player feel more unique, is create a Legacy that focuses on Artifice. It could include spells like &quot;Word of Command&quot;. Legacy attainments are usually modified versions of existing spells, but you can also modify existing attainments that the player already has and improve them a bit. So in the Legacy we're talking about, maybe the 4th or 5th attainment would be a slightly improved version of the Imbue Item attainment. For instance, the Imbue Item attainment costs mana equal to the rating of all Arcana used in the spell. But legacy attainments specifically say that if the cost would be more than 1 mana, it becomes 1 mana. So there you have it. A legacy attainment that is a cheaper version of the normal Imbue Item.<br /> <br /> Another thing you can do, is let him have a mentor that is an enchanter, and have the mentor craft and imbue items while the character assists. This way, he will still participate in the procedure, but it will also be justified for the items themselves to be created.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T06:25:15-07:00","id":1332808,"title":"","content":"As to the lack of magical crafting being unique to Prime 4, Prime 4 is the only truly sufficient way to create an item that can be used to cast spells in and of itself. However, any mage can cast spells upon objects. Some spells are more useful than others (Matter being the obvious secondary choice for crafters) to have on an object, but it should be noted that there is a distinction between an imbued item and an enhanced item. An enhanced item is &quot;magical&quot; in that it has a spell cast upon it, but enhanced items can't cast spells. The dnd equivalent would be comparing a +3 holy longsword to a magic staff that anyone could use. They're not the same at all.<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that unless you have a lot of skill in other arcana, your crafter is going to end up imbuing Prime spells into their products since they will have focused so much into Prime. Also, unless the crafter intends on having the spell in the item taking up a spell control slot, then they will also have to release the spell, for which safely releasing is really the only good option (thus costing a willpower dot (aka, 1xp)). <br /> <br /> So you can see that crafting a good imbued item isn't as easy as just having Prime 4. Your player isn't going to be able to craft imbued items immediately, which is a good thing. It'll be more special when they can do it. They should also understand that if they're going to &quot;sell&quot; an imbued item, they should ask for something decently significant in return (because investing your will into an object isn't a small thing (represented by the cost of a willpower dot)).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T07:28:02-07:00","id":1332811,"title":"","content":"You can make enhanced items without needing to use Imbued Item/Stored Spell rules. Just cast a spell that modifies/enchants the object itself, rather than trying to make a magical item to casts spells itself.<br /> <br /> Making an invisible sword can be done with just Forces Shielding on a sword, a better sword can be made with Matter Ruling/Perfecting, and a sword that is also a phone is Matter Weaving. A bonsi tree that makes tiny chicken-egg-like fruit is just life weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-27-2019, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T07:59:47-07:00","id":1332815,"title":"","content":"Looking back on what you wrote, Erebe, it seems that your player's expectations were off a little bit. Discussing this outside of the game is probably a good idea. However, resolving this in game is usually best done via role play rather than changing rules. If he gets a grasp of how prestigious being able to craft imbued items is, he may be more willing to accept enhanced items as something that doesn't require Prime.<br /> <br /> Also, the suggestion of having his character join a magic crafting legacy is a great idea. While the benefits of attainments he gets with it could help with actually crafting magic items, the philisophical standpoint is something you'll want to go over with him. Legacies aren't just smaller cliques/cults that you join to get extra powers, they are ways to alter your perspective on life itself. There's plenty to mine there for role playing. Also, if the legacy has Matter as one of the primary Arcana then your player's Obrimos can pick up another ruling Arcana (and one that is great for magic crafting too!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T10:01:09-07:00","id":1332831,"title":"","content":"I had a character (now an NPC) with a similar bent; Prime and Matter are the two most important Arcana for this sort of thing. Matter gets more use that Prime at lower power levels, meaning an Obrimos character should probably focus their rotes and praxes in that Arcana to keep mana costs down. Short term (day or week long) boosts that are then &quot;unsafely&quot; relinquished seemed to be the most effective, minimal chance of something going wrong and generally nothing worse than deterioration of the spell if something does.<br /> <br /> The<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Forge_Masters\" target=\"_blank\"> Forge Masters</a> are a Moros crafter legacy with Prime as their Ruling Arcana and Matter as their secondary (not much of a boost for an Obrimos), and so I created the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981289-2e-legacy-thaumatech-engineers\">Thaumatech Engineers</a> as an Obrimos legacy with Matter as the Ruling Arcana; the biggest difference between the two is the Thaumatech Engineers actively try to push the envelop of Sleeper technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T11:15:58-07:00","id":1332849,"title":"","content":"I think I see the issue, there is a mix up between enhanced and imbued items. An enhanced item is one that has been altered by magic. Flying cars, bags of holding, lucky guns, a wristwatch that creates full body armor, etc. They are wondrous, but can be created by any mage with the right Arcana.<br /> <br /> Imbued item and its variations are all about making gadgets. Storing spells for others to use, specializing them, etc. So why is this good ? Firstly because you can hand them to a Sleepwalker (or Sleeper if you are discrete or don't mind the Breaking Points) to use. <br /> <br /> In addition, all uses of an imbued item count as one spell control. That is a huge advantage. If you can afford the mana, your belt of invisibility can make every mage in the Consilium invisible, the Ruling of Matter that levitates a house can create a flying city, the one that makes a bag of holding can create ones for the entire cabal, etc.<br /> <br /> If you want to focus on the crafter role, I suggest he takes an appropriate Legacy. The Forge Masters from Legacies:The Ancient are the most common. But since your player is an Obrimos, I would like to suggest these two:<br /> <br /> A 2ed conversion of the Transhuman Engineers:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/10/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-legacy.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/1...egacy.html?m=1</a><br /> <br /> The Thaumatech Engineers:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981289-2e-legacy-thaumatech-engineers\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...tech-engineers</a><br /> <br /> Lastly, don't forget to create Mysteries to let them hone their craft. A Supernal Summon that teaches them about crafting and alchemy or makes items for them if they complete certain ordeals. Have them research legendary smiths, how did they make their items? Did they use some property of the Fallen to supplement the creation? Did they mix in perfected metals or bound some kind of being to them ? Why did this cabal vanish if their journals show such promising results? Why does a blade of Dumamium tempered by the fire of an Elemental Changeling and quenched in water from the river Styx sing when its near an illusion ? Discovering those answers could be his Obsession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-28-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T11:25:43-07:00","id":1332851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332796-magic-crafting-speciality?p=1332849#post1332849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus an imbued spell has the same factors as when it was cast, so if you gathered a bunch of powerful yantras, you can replicate that powerful spell with ease, on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imbued items can't benefit from Yantra bonuses and their spells' factors are chosen by the user at the time of activation; it's the <i>Reach</i> that's set at creation, barring Flexible Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T13:32:32-07:00","id":1332874,"title":"","content":"Not sure what the dude wants, but you could houserule a Prime 3 (or even 2) attainment to make a temporary version of Imbue. Treat it the same, except it only lasts a scene per mana spent on it. (or until dawn or something like that) That would get the ball rolling earlier without doing great violence to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T14:37:02-07:00","id":1332889,"title":"","content":"Just a quick two cents, I'd assume crafters ARE rare and valued, I think signs of sorcery confirms this.<br /> <br /> But its not just ability. Its the Willpower Dot costs of some of these! Thats why crafters are valued, they spend xp on these things!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T03:39:04-07:00","id":1332952,"title":"","content":"Signs of Sorcery also includes a few spells for safely relinquishing spells for other types of resources, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T13:10:18-07:00","id":1333019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1332796-magic-crafting-speciality?p=1332851#post1332851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imbued items can't benefit from Yantra bonuses and their spells' factors are chosen by the user at the time of activation; it's the <i>Reach</i> that's set at creation, barring Flexible Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. Fixed it, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}